      "title": "Failed-stop observer blocks later starts",
      "message": "Terminal retirement correctness relies on the observer being retained after a failed stop, but Go-side state may consider it retired. Also if the stop in vellumStopSystemAppearance fails, appearanceObserver remains and a later vellumStartSystemAppearance returns early because 'if (appearanceObserver) return;', so a new Run cannot register a new token and the stale token is bound to the observer; sample then drops events since the token is inactive.",
